lican spending or a polling shift toward O'Donnell could tighten this into the Lean D range.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Susie Lee (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Nevada's 3rd District pairs two-term incumbent Susie Lee against video-game composer Marty O'Donnell, a Trump-endorsed Republican who has self-funded a competitive campaign. The district leans only slightly Democratic and has been decided by fewer than four points in each of the last two cycles, so Republicans have targeted it heavily.\n\nStill, the evidence favors Lee. She holds a large cash-on-hand advantage, the only recent poll shows her up seven, and expert raters overwhelmingly place the race at Likely D or safer, with prediction markets pricing her near 95%. The Trump PAC's decision to pull $2 million in ad reservations weakens O'Donnell's late-game reach. The forecast expects Lee to win by a solid but not landslide margin.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9366, "margin": 9.91}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9036, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9329, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9282, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9091, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.906, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9242, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.942, "margin": 10.2}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.921, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9325, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.93, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9287, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.8974, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.905, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9112, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.8961, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9316, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9282, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.9294, "margin": 10.5}